# rui Project Index

**rui** is a declarative interface library for Rust with zero dependencies. This index provides quick access to build commands, test commands, examples, and module structure.

## Quick Start

### Build Commands

```bash
# Debug build
cargo build

# Optimized build
cargo build --release

# WASM target
cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p rui --example counter
```

### Test Commands

```bash
# All tests
cargo test

# Unit tests only
cargo test --lib

# Integration tests
cargo test --test integration
cargo test --test recipes -- widget_name

# Specific test files
cargo test --test setup              # Verify Rust 1.85+ and pre-commit hook
cargo test --test layout             # Layout engine tests
cargo test --test rendering          # Rendering pipeline tests
cargo test --test interaction        # Event handling tests
cargo test --test external_driving   # Frame-stepping tests (WASM compatibility)
cargo test --test recipe_1_verification  # WASM backend verification gates

# WASM tests (require Firefox and wasm-pack)
cargo test --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
wasm-pack test --headless --firefox --test wasm_integration
```

### Key Examples (Learning Path)

Entry points for learning rui:

```bash
# 1. Counter: The simplest app (start here)
cargo run -p rui --example counter

# 2. Segmented: How to build interactive controls
cargo run -p rui --example segmented

# 3. Meter: How to build passive/read-only widgets
cargo run -p rui --example meter

# 4. Other examples
cargo run -p rui --example controls       # Showcase of widgets
cargo run -p rui --example gallery -- .   # Render to PNG
cargo run -p rui --example parity -- target/parity  # WASM reference frame
cargo run -p rui --example icon           # Generate macOS app icons
cargo run -p rui --example segmented_modified  # "Copy and Modify" verification
```

## Module Structure

| Module | Purpose | Key Files |
|--------|---------|-----------|
| **element** | UI element tree; builders for structure and containers | `src/element.rs` |
| **widgets** | Recipes: button, text, title, panel, tabs, draw, segmented, meter | `src/widgets.rs` |
| **style** | Layout and appearance: Length, Radius, Tone, Align, Justify | `src/style.rs` |
| **layout** | Flexbox-like layout engine; stacking, line wrapping, scroll, layer | `src/layout.rs` |
| **paint** | Drawing abstraction: Painter API used by all elements | `src/paint.rs` |
| **canvas** | Pixel buffer and rasteriser; Canvas::draw is the root operation | `src/canvas.rs` |
| **text** | TrueType parser, glyph rasterising, text layout with kerning/ligatures | `src/text.rs` (in font/) |
| **color** | RGB(A) colors and sRGB gamma handling | `src/color.rs` |
| **geom** | Primitives: Rect, Point, Size, Insets | `src/geom.rs` |
| **image** | PNG encoder for rendering to files | `src/image.rs` |
| **input** | Input events and per-frame view of them; immediate-mode queries | `src/input.rs` |
| **theme** | Colors, spacing, type sizes; Appearance (light/dark), Tone (semantic roles) | `src/theme.rs` |
| **syntax** | Syntax highlighting tokenizer; Rust, Python, JavaScript, Bash, Diff | `src/syntax.rs` |
| **shell** | Platform window management: macOS/Windows/X11/WASM backends | `src/shell/mod.rs`, `src/shell/platform/*.rs` |
| **shell/clock** | Platform-agnostic clock abstraction (Instant on native, performance.now() on WASM) | `src/shell/clock.rs` |
| **memory** | Stateful interaction data: hover, focus, scroll, caret, animations | `src/memory.rs` |
| **app** | Application entry point; couples state, view function, and event loop | `src/app.rs` |
| **testing** | Harness: drives real frame with synthetic font for deterministic testing | `src/testing/harness.rs` |
| **demo** | Counter app; referenced by examples/counter.rs, src/wasm.rs, examples/parity.rs | `src/demo.rs` |

## Platform Backends

All platforms implement the `Backend` trait (`src/shell/mod.rs`):

| Platform | Status | File | Notes |
|----------|--------|------|-------|
| macOS | ✓ Stable | `src/shell/platform/macos.rs` | Native Cocoa window, event loop |
| Windows | ✓ Stable | `src/shell/platform/windows.rs` | Native WinAPI window, event loop |
| X11 | ✓ Stable | `src/shell/platform/x11.rs` | X11/Wayland server, event loop |
| WASM | ✓ Implemented | `src/shell/platform/wasm.rs` | Browser canvas, requestAnimationFrame |

## Key Architectural Patterns

### The View Pattern

```rust
// State: Your application data
struct App { counter: i32 }

// View: Pure function from state to UI
fn view(app: &App) -> El<App> {
    col((
        text(app.counter.to_string()),
        button("Increment", |app: &mut App| app.counter += 1),
    ))
}

// Run: Attach state and view to the event loop
App { counter: 0 }.run(view)
```

### Handlers (Not Closures)

Handlers receive mutable state as an argument, eliminating `Rc<RefCell<>>`:

```rust
.on_click(|app: &mut App| {
    app.counter += 1;  // Direct mutation; no interior mutability needed
})
```

### Testing with Harness

Drive the real frame without a window, with synthetic fonts for deterministic testing:

```rust
use rui::testing::Harness;

let mut harness = Harness::new(App { counter: 0 }, view);
harness.click_text("Increment");
assert_eq!(harness.state().counter, 1);
assert!(harness.frame().shows("1"));
```

## Test Files Reference

| Test File | Command | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| `tests/setup.rs` | `cargo test --test setup` | Rust 1.85+ and pre-commit hook verification |
| `tests/layout.rs` | `cargo test --test layout` | Flexbox-like layout engine tests |
| `tests/rendering.rs` | `cargo test --test rendering` | Rendering pipeline (colors, shapes, text) |
| `tests/recipes.rs` | `cargo test --test recipes -- widget_name` | Widget examples: checkbox, switch, slider, radio, tooltip, segmented, meter |
| `tests/interaction.rs` | `cargo test --test interaction -- --nocapture` | Clicks, drags, keyboard, focus management |
| `tests/integration.rs` | `cargo test --test integration` | End-to-end layout + rendering + interaction |
| `tests/external_driving.rs` | `cargo test --test external_driving` | Frame-stepping without event loop (WASM compat) |
| `tests/recipe_1_verification.rs` | `cargo test --test recipe_1_verification` | WASM backend verification gates |
| `tests/wasm_integration.rs` | `wasm-pack test --headless --firefox` | Browser integration tests |
| `tests/wasm_events.rs` | `wasm-pack test --headless --firefox` | WASM DOM event handling |
| `tests/wasm_fonts.rs` | `wasm-pack test --headless --firefox` | WASM font loading and rendering |
| `tests/wasm_parity.rs` | `cargo test --test wasm_parity` | Pixel-perfect native/WASM comparison |

## Common Workflows

### Run All Tests

```bash
cargo test
```

### Verify Code Quality (Pre-Commit)

```bash
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
```

### Generate Documentation

```bash
cargo doc --no-deps --open
```

### Build WASM Package

```bash
# Install dependencies (one-time)
rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
curl https://rustwasm.org/wasm-pack/installer/init.sh -sSf | sh

# Build
cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p rui --example counter
wasm-pack build --target web --release --out-dir pkg
```

### Test WASM Parity (Pixel-Perfect)

```bash
# Build native reference frame
cargo run -p rui --example parity -- target/parity

# Build WASM
wasm-pack build --target web --release --out-dir pkg

# Serve locally
python3 -m http.server 8731 --bind 127.0.0.1

# Open http://127.0.0.1:8731/examples/parity.html in browser
# Green = identical, Red = differences
```

## Recipes

Recipes are step-by-step implementations of major features with verification gates.

### Recipe 1: Adding a WASM Backend

**Status:** Implemented (18 commits across 3 phases)

**Phases:**
1. Clock abstraction (`src/shell/clock.rs`) — Platform-agnostic time measurement
2. FrameDriver refactor — Extract core loop into reusable `turn()` function
3. WASM integration — Implement Backend trait for browser, wire events via DOM

**Verification gates:**
- `cargo test --lib` — Unit tests pass
- `cargo test --test external_driving -- state_mut_between_frames_drives_the_next_frame` — Frame-stepping works
- `cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p rui --example counter` — WASM compiles
- `wasm-pack test --headless --firefox` — Browser tests pass
- `cargo test --test wasm_parity` — Pixel-perfect parity confirmed

### Recipe 2: Add a New Widget

**Pattern:**
1. Define state and appearance
2. Write widget function in `src/widgets.rs` (build El<S> from primitives)
3. Add test in `tests/recipes.rs` (use Harness)
4. Verify `cargo test --test recipes -- widget_name`
5. Run example to confirm visually

**Examples to copy:**
- `segmented` (interactive choice selector, 59 lines)
- `meter` (passive progress bar, 22 lines)
- checkbox, switch, slider, radio (in tests/recipes.rs)

## Verification Checklist

Before committing:

- [ ] `cargo build` succeeds
- [ ] `cargo test` passes (all tests)
- [ ] `cargo fmt --check` passes (no formatting issues)
- [ ] `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes (no lints)
- [ ] Examples run without errors: `cargo run -p rui --example counter`
- [ ] For WASM changes: `cargo test --test recipe_1_verification` passes

## Troubleshooting Quick Links

- **Build fails:** Check Rust version (`rustc --version` — need 1.85+), run `cargo clean`
- **Tests fail:** Read assertion message, run single test with `cargo test --lib test_name`
- **Pre-commit hook blocks commit:** Run `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy --fix` to auto-fix
- **WASM won't build:** Verify target with `rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown`
- **Examples won't run:** Verify you're in project root (`pwd`), check platform support (macOS/Windows/X11 for native)
- **X11 display error on Linux:** Ensure X11 is running (`echo $DISPLAY`) or use `xvfb-run -a`

## Entry Points by Role

| Role | Start Here |
|------|-----------|
| **Learning rui** | `cargo run -p rui --example counter`, then read `CLAUDE.md` |
| **Building widgets** | Copy `examples/segmented.rs` (interactive) or `examples/meter.rs` (passive), modify, test with `Harness` |
| **Platform hacking** | Read `src/shell/mod.rs` (Backend trait), then `src/shell/platform/*.rs` for your target OS |
| **Font rendering** | Read `src/font/` modules; `tests/rendering.rs` shows text layout tests |
| **Layout engine** | Read `src/layout.rs` and `tests/layout.rs` for flexbox-like stacking and wrapping |
| **WASM porting** | Read Recipe 1 commits; verify with `cargo test --test recipe_1_verification` |
| **Testing** | Use `Harness` in `tests/recipes.rs` examples; see `src/testing/harness.rs` for API |

## Finished

Finished means every gate below exits 0. Scouts write items only for failing, unknown, or suspect gates, tagged [cap: <id>].

::code id=cap-build lang=bash run reads=src,examples,tests,Cargo.toml
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
T=$(command -v gtimeout || command -v timeout)
log=$(mktemp)
if $T 300 cargo build --all-targets > "$log" 2>&1; then
  echo "cap-build PASS: cargo build --all-targets (lib, examples, tests, benches) exited 0"
  exit 0
else
  echo "cap-build FAIL: cargo build --all-targets exited nonzero"
  tail -20 "$log"
  exit 1
fi
::end

::code id=cap-tests lang=bash run reads=src,Cargo.toml
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
T=$(command -v gtimeout || command -v timeout)
log=$(mktemp)
set +e
$T 300 cargo test --lib > "$log" 2>&1
code=$?
set -e
result_line=$(grep -E "^test result:" "$log" | tail -1)
passed=$(echo "$result_line" | grep -oE '[0-9]+ passed' | awk '{print $1}')
if [ "$code" -eq 0 ] && [ "${passed:-0}" -ge 390 ]; then
  echo "cap-tests PASS: cargo test --lib passed with $passed tests"
  exit 0
fi
echo "cap-tests FAIL: expected 390+ tests to pass, got ${passed:-0}, code=$code"
tail -20 "$log"
exit 1
::end

::code id=cap-examples lang=bash run reads=examples,src,Cargo.toml
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
T=$(command -v gtimeout || command -v timeout)
count=$(find examples -maxdepth 1 -name "*.rs" -type f | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
if [ "$count" -lt 2 ]; then
  echo "cap-examples FAIL: only $count example file(s) found (need >= 2)"
  exit 1
fi
log=$(mktemp)
# On Windows, use --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu to work around MSVC linker issues
BUILD_CMD="cargo build --examples"
if uname -s | grep -q MINGW; then
  BUILD_CMD="cargo build --examples --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu"
fi
if $T 300 $BUILD_CMD > "$log" 2>&1; then
  echo "cap-examples PASS: $count example files, cargo build --examples exited 0"
  exit 0
else
  echo "cap-examples FAIL: cargo build --examples exited nonzero"
  tail -20 "$log"
  exit 1
fi
::end

::code id=cap-clippy lang=bash run reads=src,examples,tests,Cargo.toml
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
T=$(command -v gtimeout || command -v timeout)
log=$(mktemp)
if $T 300 cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings > "$log" 2>&1; then
  echo "cap-clippy PASS: cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings exited 0"
  exit 0
else
  echo "cap-clippy FAIL: cargo clippy exited nonzero"
  tail -20 "$log"
  exit 1
fi
::end

::code id=cap-fmt lang=bash run reads=src,examples,tests,Cargo.toml
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
if cargo fmt --all -- --check > /dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo "cap-fmt PASS: cargo fmt --all -- --check passed (source is formatted)"
  exit 0
else
  echo "cap-fmt FAIL: unformatted files detected"
  cargo fmt --all -- --check
  exit 1
fi
::end

::code id=cap-recipes lang=bash run reads=tests/recipes.rs,src,Cargo.toml
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
T=$(command -v gtimeout || command -v timeout)
log=$(mktemp)
if $T 300 cargo test --test recipes > "$log" 2>&1; then
  passed=$(grep -E "^test result:" "$log" | tail -1 | grep -oE '[0-9]+ passed' | awk '{print $1}')
  echo "cap-recipes PASS: cargo test --test recipes passed $passed tests"
  exit 0
else
  echo "cap-recipes FAIL: cargo test --test recipes exited nonzero"
  tail -20 "$log"
  exit 1
fi
::end
